<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Git Forensics</title>
<style>
  body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0f172a;color:#e2e8f0;padding:18px}
  h1{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 8px;color:#93c5fd}
  p,li{font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.5}
  pre{background:#1e293b;color:#e2e8f0;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.78rem;overflow:auto}
  code{background:#1e293b;color:#fde68a;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}
  a{color:#7dd3fc}
</style></head><body>
  <h1>🕵️ Git history forensics</h1>
  <p>A staging token was committed and later rotated out. Rebuild the repo and find the commit
  that <strong>introduced</strong> it.</p>
  <p><a download="history.fastimport" href="data:application/octet-stream;base64,">⬇️ Download history.fastimport</a></p>
  <p>Rebuild and investigate:</p>
  <pre>mkdir repo && cd repo && git init -q
git fast-import --quiet &lt; ../history.fastimport
git checkout -f main

# find where the token entered history
git log -p -- config/app.env
# or pinpoint it:
git log -S 'STAGING_TOKEN=' --oneline -- config/app.env</pre>
  <p>Submit JSON with the recovered token and the <em>subject line</em> of the commit that
  introduced it:</p>
  <pre>{"token": "stg_...", "commit_subject": "..."}</pre>
</body></html>